WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.663
How.

2
00:00:00.663 --> 00:00:05.687
Personnel actions drive the three
identity events, by code, not by ticket.

3
00:00:05.687 --> 00:00:09.413
A joiner gets an account and
baseline access ready on day one.

4
00:00:09.413 --> 00:00:12.453
A mover has the old
assignment's access removed,

5
00:00:12.453 --> 00:00:15.962
the new baseline applied,
and any exceptions reviewed.

6
00:00:15.962 --> 00:00:17.869
And a leaver is blocked first:

7
00:00:17.869 --> 00:00:22.951
the account disabled and sessions
revoked at the effective separation time,

8
00:00:22.951 --> 00:00:28.113
then credentials, devices and access
removed in parallel, each one reconciled.

9
00:00:28.113 --> 00:00:31.288
The book is precise about what
the platform actually does.

10
00:00:31.288 --> 00:00:34.181
Lifecycle Workflows run on one tenant-wide

11
00:00:34.181 --> 00:00:37.476
schedule and need an Entra
ID Governance license.

12
00:00:37.476 --> 00:00:40.750
Revoking sessions stops
new tokens being issued,

13
00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:44.025
but tokens already issued
last until they expire.

14
00:00:44.025 --> 00:00:47.421
Privileged leavers need their
own verified block path,

15
00:00:47.421 --> 00:00:51.850
because the built-in disable task
doesn't support users with admin roles.

16
00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:55.236
And synced users must be
deleted in Active Directory,

17
00:00:55.236 --> 00:00:57.313
or the next sync brings them back.

18
00:00:57.313 --> 00:01:02.189
Credentials follow the same events:
PIV issuance, certificate binding and

19
00:01:02.189 --> 00:01:07.300
termination, and device certificates
retired before the account is deleted.
